Actions Performed

Open Issue Track Ticket Management System and identified 3 High-Priority Tickets. Based on priority on when the ticket arrived.

Ticket# 11:
Issue: User reports the computer will not turn on upon arriving at work. 
Attempted to turn on the computer and confirmed the user issue.
Conduct a physical inspection of power cables on all computers; all are plugged in correctly, but I discovered VoIP had no power. 
Conducted a physical inspection of the power strip and found it was switched off. 
Turned on the power strip, the desktop, and the monitor. Confirmed Computer now powers on
Provided a professional comment on the ticket and closed it out.

Ticket# 12:
Issue: User reports the computer won't start, but it will make a beeping noise when it turns on.
Turned on the computer and confirmed the user issue of a series of beeps. No external observation would contribute to the beeping
The working theory is a RAM issue.
Ensured all power sources were turned off, unplugged the computer, and grounded myself
Upon opening the desktop, I verified that no RAM was installed. 
Verified the type, speed, and placement for Dual Channel against the motherboard specs. Installed 2x DDR3, 2GB 1600
Restarted the desktop into BIOS and confirmed the Memory Information of RAM specification, then booted into Windows. 
Provided a professional comment on the ticket and closed it out.

Ticket# 13:
Issue: User reports computer will turn on, but the monitor fails to display anything. 
The computer is on arrival with the monitor displaying No Signal Detected.
Conducted a physical inspection to verify cable connections. Discovered that the HDMI was disconnected from the desktop HDMI port.
Plugged the HDMI Cable back in, and the monitor regained connection. 
Provided a professional comment on the ticket and closed it out.

